### Decisions
- `wait` on wait_for_element_to_disappear(_by_xpath) is reinterpreted as the timeout for that call (None -> poll_time). It used to be a per-poll sleep. Call sites pass wait=60 / 5 meaning "wait up to N seconds".
- "Page changed" = captured <html> root stale OR fragment-stripped URL changed, then readyState complete, then one settle poll. Clicked-element staleness counts only when no root exists (Appium native), because React re-renders buttons on click.
- Legacy click_and_wait_for_* predicates keep raw element.click() retried per poll (raises on overlay interception); their success condition becomes a strict superset of the old one.
- Shadowed duplicate: keep find_and_send_modifer_key(locator, key); rename the element variant to send_modifer_key_to_element (no callers anywhere).

